#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:4
msgid "Orthogonal projections"
msgstr "Proyecciones ortogonales"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:6
msgid ""
"Spectroscopic measurements almost always contain variation that is "
"irrelevant to the property you want to predict — baseline drift, "
"temperature effects, scattering differences, instrument noise. "
"**Orthogonal projection** methods identify this unwanted systematic "
"variation and remove it before calibration, leaving a simpler, more "
"interpretable dataset for the downstream model."
msgstr ""
"Las mediciones espectroscópicas casi siempre contienen variación irrelevante "
"para la propiedad que se desea predecir: deriva de la línea base, efectos de "
"la temperatura, diferencias de dispersión y ruido instrumental. Los métodos "
"de **proyección ortogonal** identifican esta variación sistemática no deseada "
"y la eliminan antes de la calibración, lo que deja un conjunto de datos más "
"sencillo e interpretable para el modelo posterior."

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:12
msgid ""
"``chemotools`` provides three supervised orthogonal filtering methods in "
":mod:`chemotools.projection`:"
msgstr ""
"``chemotools`` proporciona tres métodos supervisados de filtrado ortogonal en "
":mod:`chemotools.projection`:"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:15
msgid ":class:`~chemotools.projection.OrthogonalSignalCorrection` (OSC)"
msgstr ":class:`~chemotools.projection.OrthogonalSignalCorrection` (OSC)"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:16
msgid ":class:`~chemotools.projection.OrthogonalPLS` (OPLS)"
msgstr ":class:`~chemotools.projection.OrthogonalPLS` (OPLS)"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:17
msgid ":class:`~chemotools.projection.DirectOrthogonalization` (DO)"
msgstr ":class:`~chemotools.projection.DirectOrthogonalization` (DO)"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:19
msgid ""
"All three are sklearn-compatible transformers: they accept ``(X, y)`` in "
"``fit`` and return a corrected ``X`` with the same number of features "
"from ``transform``. Their behaviour has been systematically compared by "
"Svensson, Kourti & MacGregor [1]_."
msgstr ""
"Los tres son transformadores compatibles con sklearn: aceptan ``(X, y)`` en "
"``fit`` y ``transform`` devuelve un ``X`` corregido con el mismo número de "
"características. Svensson, Kourti y MacGregor [1]_ compararon sistemáticamente "
"su comportamiento."

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:28
msgid ""
"A fourth method — "
":class:`~chemotools.projection.ExternalParameterOrthogonalization` (EPO) "
"— handles *unsupervised* removal of variation linked to known external "
"factors (e.g., temperature, humidity). It is covered on its own page."
msgstr ""
"Un cuarto método, "
":class:`~chemotools.projection.ExternalParameterOrthogonalization` (EPO), "
"permite eliminar de forma *no supervisada* la variación vinculada a factores "
"externos conocidos (p. ej., temperatura o humedad). Se describe en una página "
"específica."

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:34
msgid ""
"Svensson et al. [1]_ found that **none of these methods consistently "
"improve prediction accuracy** over plain PLS on raw data. Their primary "
"benefit is **model simplicity and interpretability**: the corrected data "
"requires fewer PLS components, and the removed variation can itself carry"
" useful diagnostic information about the measurement process."
msgstr ""
"Svensson et al. [1]_ observaron que **ninguno de estos métodos mejora de forma "
"sistemática la precisión de predicción** respecto a PLS sin modificaciones "
"sobre los datos sin procesar. Su principal ventaja es la **simplicidad e "
"interpretabilidad del modelo**: los datos corregidos requieren menos "
"componentes PLS y la variación eliminada puede contener información de "
"diagnóstico útil sobre el proceso de medición."

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:41
msgid "What does \"orthogonal\" mean here?"
msgstr "¿Qué significa «ortogonal» en este contexto?"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:43
msgid ""
"After fitting a model on spectra ``X`` to predict ``y``, the total "
"variance in ``X`` can be decomposed into:"
msgstr ""
"Después de ajustar un modelo con los espectros ``X`` para predecir ``y``, la "
"varianza total de ``X`` puede descomponerse en:"

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:46
msgid ""
"**Predictive variation** — correlated with ``y``, informative for the "
"model."
msgstr ""
"**Variación predictiva**: correlacionada con ``y`` e informativa para el "
"modelo."

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:47
msgid ""
"**Orthogonal variation** — uncorrelated with ``y``, systematic noise or "
"interference for the regression task."
msgstr ""
"**Variación ortogonal**: no correlacionada con ``y``; constituye ruido "
"sistemático o interferencia para la tarea de regresión."

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:50
msgid ""
"Removing orthogonal variation before building the model reduces the "
"number of PLS components needed and often makes the resulting loadings "
"easier to interpret chemically."
msgstr ""
"Eliminar la variación ortogonal antes de construir el modelo reduce el número "
"de componentes PLS necesarios y, a menudo, facilita la interpretación química "
"de las cargas resultantes."

#: ../../source/explore/orthogonal_projections.rst:54
msgid "Predictive vs orthogonal variation in a spectrum"
msgstr "Variación predictiva frente a ortogonal en un espectro"

